# Design principles

Use .ai/skills/design-principles as the complete reference.

- Use concrete, pronounceable English names.
- Avoid helper, util, manager, data, info, temp and x names.
- Functions have one responsibility and verb names.
- Avoid boolean flags that switch behavior.
- Use guard clauses and low indentation.
- Follow CQS: commands mutate and return void; queries return values and do not mutate.
- Use DomainError factory methods for domain failures.
- Return Maybe for optional domain values.
- Prefer composition over inheritance.
- No JS getters/setters or underscore private prefixes.
